    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Kyle Tucker** (75.81) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) leading the charge, both benefiting significantly from favorable matchups against Lorenzen and Gallen, respectively. **Tucker** remains our most reliable asset against a high-xERA opponent, while **Merrill** capitalizes on a stellar 19% SP skill boost and a favorable batting order position. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) is also a standout play, as his efficiency is buoyed by a 14% dynamic platoon advantage against Imai. The focus on high-efficiency, speed-oriented targets remains paramount; notably, **Nasim Nunez** (60.95) stays in the starting lineup despite a lower base projection because his unique combination of a slow opposing SP delivery and a 3% boost from his switch-hitting profile provides critical SB upside that offsets his mid-order ranking.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Miguel Vargas**, who sits on the bench with a 53.32 score despite elite underlying metrics, specifically a 0.406 xwOBA. While **Vargas** offers a strong lead-off profile, he was edged out by **Curtis Mead** (60.76) and **Gunnar Henderson** (57.32), as the optimizer favored their specific platoon advantages and the high run-scoring probability inherent in their respective batting orders. Meanwhile, we must exercise caution with **Josh Lowe** (49.19) and **Drake Baldwin** (43.62); both face elite arms in deGrom and Skenes. **Lowe** is particularly hindered by an elite hold SP, which suppresses his SB potential, while **Baldwin** faces a significant 19% SP skill penalty. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** (47.68) closely as he navigates a matchup against Woo, but his premium position at the top of the order keeps his floor secure enough to warrant a start.",
